from ./Segmentation import Segmentation
from ./Tokens import Tokens
from ./WordClasses import WordClasses
from ./StatementParts import StatementParts

export anchor Text:
    description:
        Prose is where most of a specification's meaning lives, and where it
        is least precise. This chapter covers how analysis takes a block of
        prose apart, from paragraphs down to single words, and then puts the
        pieces back together as statements with a known shape.

        Nothing in this chapter decides what anything means. It only finds
        the pieces that meaning will be built from in the next chapter.

    steps:
        ```text
        segment     paragraphs into sentences, and sentences into statements
        tokenize    statements into words, numbers, references and punctuation
        classify    each word as a noun, verb, adjective and so on
        find parts  what the statement is about, what it says, and when
        ```

        The steps are described in @{Segmentation}, @{Tokens},
        @{WordClasses} and @{StatementParts}.
